  "review_notes": [
    "The final Hebrew clause literally means “as thy hand shall find.” The ASV recasts the possessor as the subject (“thou”), the third-person verb as “shalt find,” and “hand” as “occasion”; the alignment preserves those distinct correspondences.",
    "The ASV’s “when” is treated as added under rule 55 because no Hebrew subordinator licenses it."
